            <ArticleTitle>A cistrome roadmap for understanding pancreatic islet biology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/ng.2880</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although dozens of common variants have been associated with increased risk of type 2 diabetes (T2D), the mechanisms by which these variants increase disease susceptibility are largely unknown. A new study mapping the human pancreatic islet cistrome provides a roadmap for exploring the effects of these variants and suggests that altered enhancer function might be a common contributor to the genetic risk of T2D.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
